#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:5
#: 9fc70a55308448dfac5f83f9e0692e7c
msgid "OSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:10
#: f34b48390b11409b8cf74d0f731f07b3
msgid "OSD functionality is provided for on-board OSDs using MAX7456-type chips and external MSP based OSDs, including DJI Goggles, and goggles using DisplayPort. This enables overlay of FC data on the video. Once enabled, it uses various panel items that can individually be set active and positioned on the screen using respective parameters. It allows to setup multiple screen layouts and switch between those using a spare RC channel. It also allows the display and change of sets of parameters using stick gestures or RC transmitters, in certain cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:15
#: b7c5b5f014114e13ad3f42423007df24
msgid "Being an integral library of ArduPilot firmware, the OSD code provides the prerequisites to be redirected to various backends other than MAX-type chipsets, including testing on SITL setups without actual autopilot- or video-hardware needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:18
#: f06fca1b70f142a2b24117c45eee80e3
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:20
#: 9b73cbb136be41fba15be13e841dc105
msgid "To enable the OSD overlay on MAX7456-type chips, set parameter: ``OSD_TYPE`` to 1, reboot and reload parameters. This exposes the whole OSD parameter group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:23
#: f296eb2c25454a80906cef849107eb56
msgid "To set a RC channel for screen switching, use parameter ``OSD_CHAN``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:25
#: 5b913e3b85674012a4d3e6ab6965f99f
msgid "To set the units used to display, use parameter ``OSD_UNITS``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:27
#: bbb990b9ea4241069f08d9c04088bf17
msgid "``0`` = Metric (meters,kilometers,meters/sec,kilometers/hour,degs in C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:28
#: 5a3494d302344e8d8c234888ed5265bc
msgid "``1`` = Imperial (feet, miles, feet/sec, miles/hour, degs in F)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:29
#: 27340094e29b4651856977ab496215a7
msgid "``2`` = ArduPilot Native (meters,kilometers,meters/sec,degs in C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:30
#: 06fd43b711e94d2bb24ab03869bce5e8
msgid "``3`` = Aviation (feet, nautical mile, feet/min, knots, degs in C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:32
#: 01f3c96373264e448f5b082e48b94af2
msgid "To set vertical and horizontal display offset (space at top and left side of screen), use parameters ``OSD_H_OFFSET``, ``OSD_V_OFFSET``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:34
#: 6b67049143f043a0abe5f392bfd0af0d
msgid "Several options can be set using :ref:`OSD_OPTIONS<OSD_OPTIONS>` (bitmask selection):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:36
#: dde67f55b3ca48b880c745fafdff49b3
msgid "bit0 = Enable use of compact number+decimal point fonts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:37
#: 4189740e24714e24814bbe03084d5524
msgid "bit1 = Invert wind direction indicator (to point to the direction its blowing from instead of toward)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:38
#: 55827a96437f4adeada5a43f67aeb4db
msgid "bit2 = Invert horizon roll direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:39
#: 1265404ac74f4517b154110eb3ce5767
msgid "bit3 = Convert feet to miles at 5280ft instead of 10000ft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:40
#: 12960eef1f6e41668ddf8dca1d67c5ae
msgid "bit4 = Do not display crosshair"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:41
#: f2789535355940d39b04f29d134ac565
msgid "bit5 = Translate arrow directions when using BF font set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:42
#: ffad55f760aa48b9b61e92e47e8fdde4
msgid "bit6 = Aviation style horizon when inverted (pitch moves horizon in opposite direction)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:44
#: 854b9445881c46ab8c22d53755b9a390
msgid "Several font sets are included and can be changed during runtime (and those who can build the software can customize or add additional font sets....see libraries/AP_OSD/fonts/README.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:46
#: 4af0ef6215374c03a6a3cfa6313039e2
msgid ":ref:`OSD_FONT<OSD_FONT>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:48
#: 4f28258aa6f9493e96fe0e07590be00c
msgid "``0`` = Clarity (default). A clearly visible large font"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:49
#: 6d98232410db4bfa94ff46db7a61b0e0
msgid "``1`` = Clarity Medium. Good visibility, less dominant than clarity default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:50
#: 465c8cd0cb204094a035475e5285d0d5
msgid "``2`` = Betaflight.  bf- / inav-osd default style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:51
#: b1769e5ae0dc4d22a8998fd36306756e
msgid "``3`` = Bold. A bolder version of Betaflight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:52
#: 3a823ce43c0c41f7b9588334b223ced7
msgid "``4`` = Digital. 80's LED clock radio style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:54
#: a643612c3fce4c7e9f52a4219e5ea9a8
msgid "Onboard font options might be limited on 1 MB boards to save memory for other features. However, font upload from SD card is supported. This allows the user to choose from up to 10 font files (named \"font0.bin\" - \"font9.bin\") placed in the root directory of your SD card. Additionally, this allows the user to easily add individualized and/or customized language charsets for the onboard OSD without the need to compile  individual firmware. Runtime font changing using the parameter :ref:`OSD_FONT<OSD_FONT>` is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:56
#: f48bca7f04f54bfc8c894b74a9ceca42
msgid "MAVftp might be a convenient option to upload files to your SD card without having to physically remove it from your autopilot. Font files, font editor, and utilities to convert to a .bin file from .mcm are `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_OSD/fonts>`__. If downloading the editor or a font's .bin file from this site, be sure to use the ``Download`` button, rather than selecting ``Raw``, and then right click saving, as you would the .mcm or .py files."
msgstr ""

